<% content_for :title, "GEO by Mod Op" %>
<div id="container" class="case">
    <p class="crumb"><a href="/nexus">&larr; Back to Nexus platform</a></p>
    <section id="cs-top">
        <h1>GEO by Mod Op</h1>
        <h2>Brand visibility across AI answer engines, delivered through a free audit and a paid optimization program. It runs today at <a href="https://geo.modop.ai" target="_blank">geo.modop.ai</a>.</h2>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-situation">
        <h3>The situation</h3>
        <p>Buyers no longer start only at search results. They ask ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity directly, and those engines return a synthesized answer. A brand can rank first in Google and still be invisible in that answer, with no equivalent of a rank tracker to explain why. Agencies were selling SEO retainers into a channel that had already partly moved.</p>
        <p>Inside Orion, GEO/AEO surfaced from the Launchpad prototype pipeline as one of the first priority concepts. It was the first portfolio product that needed to stand on its own as something a client would pay for.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-role">
        <h3>What I owned</h3>
        <p>I directed GEO's product design and build. Working with subject-matter experts, I defined the audit and scoring framework, then designed how GEO integrated with and fed data into Mod Op's AI platform. I aligned stakeholders through the build and supported go-to-market, including the funnel from free audit to paid program.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-audit">
        <h3>The audit</h3>
        <p>The free tool runs a substantive audit. It combines brand research with prompt testing across ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity. The report scores GEO readiness, compares branded and unbranded visibility, measures citation share, and ranks the brand against named competitors.</p>
        <figure class="report-figure">
            <%= image_tag "geo-audit-glance.png", alt: "GEO audit summary card for Apple: score 65 of 100, competitive and gaining ground, 100% branded visibility, 81% unbranded visibility, 38% unbranded citation share, #1 brand vs. competitors" %>
            <figcaption>A live audit run against Apple, a neutral example, not a client engagement.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>The report doesn't stop at a score. It shows the specific prompts a brand shows up for and the ones it's missing from, which competitors are winning the questions buyers actually ask, and where each engine currently stands on citing the brand at all.</p>
        <figure class="report-figure">
            <%= image_tag "geo-audit-shareofvoice.png", alt: "Share of AI voice ranking showing Apple first at 81%, ahead of Samsung Galaxy S26, Google Pixel 10, and six other named competitors" %>
            <figcaption>Competitor ranking by share of AI voice, pulled directly from the answer engines.</figcaption>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-framework">
        <h3>The GEO Periodic Table</h3>
        <p>Underneath the score is a proprietary framework of 25 ranking factors. They cover content quality, structured data, brand and entity signals, trustworthiness, performance, and engagement. Every factor maps to something a site owner can fix, turning the diagnostic into a prioritized plan.</p>
        <figure class="report-figure">
            <%= image_tag "geo-periodic-table.png", alt: "The GEO Periodic Table: 25 ranking factors grouped into six categories, each scored and mapped to a specific improvement" %>
            <figcaption>The scoring framework the audit is built on, shown here at 5 of 12 on AEO readiness.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>The report closes with an executive summary of current visibility and competitive standing, followed by the most important fixes.</p>
        <figure class="report-figure">
            <%= image_tag "geo-audit-execsummary.png", alt: "Executive summary of the GEO audit: where you're visible, how you compare, where you're missing, and what to do first" %>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-funnel">
        <h3>The funnel</h3>
        <p>The free audit is the top of the funnel. It has to be useful enough for someone to finish and share internally. The full engagement adds a deeper baseline, a cross-channel activation plan, and ongoing scoring across all 25 Periodic Table factors.</p>
        <figure class="report-figure">
            <%= image_tag "geo-program-cta.png", alt: "GEO Program upsell: Audit & Baseline, Cross-Channel Activation Plan, and Periodic Table Scoring, offered at the end of the free report" %>
        </figure>
    </section>

    <section id="cs-learned">
        <h3>What I learned</h3>
        <p>A free diagnostic only works as a funnel when it gives a useful answer. Withholding the real value erodes the trust needed for a paid next step. Designing GEO meant deciding what the audit should resolve immediately and what required an ongoing program.</p>
    </section>

    <p class="crumb"><a href="/nexus">&larr; Back to Nexus platform</a></p>
</div>
